# observation groups — a family, the zoom into one member, and a container's contents
#
# The farm orchard holds four fruit trees, each holding a fruit and a branch. Four trees are one kind,
# so the opener is offered "the trees here" rather than each tree, and after looking at them its next
# look goes to one of them (the zoom) instead of to something unrelated in the orchard. A tree holds
# two different things, so directing attention to it renders its contents one by one.
#
# No --observe-only: that flag switches groups off, so the scripts pinned by it keep reaching exactly
# the object they name.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type farm --location-id 1 --start-area Orchard --period afternoon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# The family, then one of its members.
expect drawn to
expect the trees here. There are several
expect shifts to an apple tree

# Attention directed to the tree: its contents, not the tree again.
click keyword tree
choose 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect My attention is drawn to a branch
expect shifts to an apple.
quit
